ena Aurea","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b1":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily I, on Acts 1:1–3","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"He recovered them by His discourses concerning the future.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210101.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b2":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily I, on Acts 1:4–5","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"Christ did not suffer these to appear in the field before the descent of the Spirit.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210101.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b3":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily II, on Acts 1:6–8","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"He raised up their souls.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210102.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b4":{"kind":"catena_aurea","pericope_ids":["catena.luke.24.50"],"source":"Catena Aurea","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b5":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily II, on Acts 1:9","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"This too was a sure sign that He went up to Heaven.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210102.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b6":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily II, on Acts 1:10","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"their words moreover were calculated for soothing.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210102.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b7":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Robert Witham, in Haydock","work":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","locus":"Acts 1:11","verbatim_excerpt":"he ascended by his own power … will he come by his own power to judge the world.","source_url":"https://haydockcommentary.com/acts-of-apostles-1","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b8":{"kind":"catena_aurea","pericope_ids":["catena.matthew.28.16"],"source":"Catena Aurea","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b9":{"kind":"catena_aurea","pericope_ids":["catena.matthew.28.16"],"source":"Catena Aurea","status":"APPROVED"},"glo2.b10":{"kind":"catena_aurea","pericope_ids":["catena.mark.16.19"],"source":"Catena Aurea","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b1":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily III, on Acts 1:12–14","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"For this is a powerful weapon in temptations.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210103.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b2":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Robert Witham, in Haydock","work":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","locus":"Acts 2:1","verbatim_excerpt":"were all of one mind.","source_url":"https://haydockcommentary.com/acts-of-apostles-2","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b3":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Augustin Calmet, in Haydock","work":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","locus":"Acts 2:2","verbatim_excerpt":"disposed them to receive the gift of heaven with humility and fervour.","source_url":"https://haydockcommentary.com/acts-of-apostles-2","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b4":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"John Stephen Menochius, in Haydock","work":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","locus":"Acts 2:3","verbatim_excerpt":"the efficacy of the apostles’ preaching","source_url":"https://haydockcommentary.com/acts-of-apostles-2","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b5":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily IV, on Acts 2:1–4","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"not merely received the grace of the Spirit, but ‘were filled.’","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210104.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b6":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily IV, on Acts 2:5–6","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"The multitude was confounded.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210104.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b7":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily IV, on Acts 2:9–11","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"mark how they run from east to west","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210104.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b8":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily V, on Acts 2:14","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"see here his boldness, and his great freedom of speech.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210105.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b9":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily VII, on Acts 2:37–38","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"Not merely were they persuaded; they even condemned themselves … when the delinquent has confessed, then is he saved!","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210107.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo3.b10":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Chrysostom","work":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","locus":"Homily VII, on Acts 2:41–42","translator":"J. Walker, J. Sheppard and H. Browne; rev. George B. Stevens","verbatim_excerpt":"Here are two virtues, perseverance and concord.","source_url":"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/210107.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homilies on the Acts of the Apostles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b1":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Alphonsus Maria de Liguori","work":"The Glories of Mary","locus":"Discourse VIII, Another Discourse on the Assumption of Mary","edition":"Second American Edition, 1852 English translation","source_kind":"Marian typological commentary","verbatim_excerpt":"bring with thee also the living ark of thy sanctification, namely, thy mother","source_url":"https://www.ecatholic2000.com/liguori/glories/glories37.shtml","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"The Glories of Mary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b2":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Alphonsus Maria de Liguori","work":"The Glories of Mary","locus":"Discourse VIII, Another Discourse on the Assumption of Mary","edition":"Second American Edition, 1852 English translation","source_kind":"Explicit Marian Assumption application","verbatim_excerpt":"Come, my dear mother","source_url":"https://www.ecatholic2000.com/liguori/glories/glories37.shtml","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"The Glories of Mary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b3":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Alphonsus Maria de Liguori","work":"The Glories of Mary","locus":"Discourse VIII, Another Discourse on the Assumption of Mary","edition":"Second American Edition, 1852 English translation","source_kind":"Explicit Marian Assumption application","verbatim_excerpt":"leave that valley of tears","source_url":"https://www.ecatholic2000.com/liguori/glories/glories37.shtml","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"The Glories of Mary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b4":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Alphonsus Maria de Liguori","work":"The Glories of Mary","locus":"Discourse VIII, Another Discourse on the Assumption of Mary","edition":"historical English translation, reproduced from The Glories of Mary","source_kind":"Explicit Marian Assumption application","verbatim_excerpt":"Come with soul and body","source_url":"https://www.immaculatalibrary.com/snippets/2021-09-03-the-glorious-entry-of-mary-into-heaven-accompanied-by-angels.html","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"The Glories of Mary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b5":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Bernard of Clairvaux","work":"Sermons on the Canticle of Canticles","locus":"Sermon LXI, on Canticles 2:14","source_kind":"Direct spiritual commentary on the verse","verbatim_excerpt":"interpreting the “clefts of the rock” to mean the Wounds of Christ","source_url":"https://www.ecatholic2000.com/bernard/sermons-canticles-vol-2.shtml","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Sermons on the Canticle of Canticles","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b6":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Robert Bellarmine","work":"A Commentary on the Book of Psalms","locus":"Psalm 44, verse 10","translator":"Ven. John O’Sullivan, D.D.","edition":"James Duffy & Co., 1866 English translation","source_kind":"Direct commentary with explicit Marian application","verbatim_excerpt":"particularly the Blessed Virgin ... holds the first place among the members of the Church","source_url":"https://www.ecatholic2000.com/bellarmine/commentary-on-psalms.shtml","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"A Commentary on the Book of Psalms","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b7":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Eudes","work":"The Admirable Heart of Mary","locus":"Part Six, Chapter I: “All the Glory of the King’s Daughter Is Within”","source_kind":"Explicit Marian commentary on Psalm 44:14","verbatim_excerpt":"the admirable Heart of Mary is a source of benefactions without number","source_url":"https://www.liberius.net/livres/The_admirable_Heart_of_Mary_000000374.pdf","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"The Admirable Heart of Mary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b8":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Pope Pius XII","work":"Munificentissimus Deus","locus":"§26","source_kind":"Magisterial Marian typological witness to the Ark motif","verbatim_excerpt":"a type of the most pure body of the Virgin Mary","source_url":"https://www.vatican.va/content/pius-xii/en/apost_constitutions/documents/hf_p-xii_apc_19501101_munificentissimus-deus.html","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Munificentissimus Deus","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b9":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Bishop Richard Challoner, in Haydock","work":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","locus":"Apocalypse 12:1","source_kind":"Direct commentary with explicit Marian application","verbatim_excerpt":"It may also, by allusion, be applied to our blessed Lady.","source_url":"https://haydockcommentary.com/apocalypse-12","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo4.b10":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Pope Leo XIII","work":"Augustissimae Virginis Mariae","locus":"§12","source_kind":"Papal Marian/Rosary application of Judith 13:23–25","verbatim_excerpt":"this perennial stream of praise ... was foretold","source_url":"https://www.vatican.va/content/leo-xiii/en/encyclicals/documents/hf_l-xiii_enc_12091897_augustissimae-virginis-mariae.html","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Augustissimae Virginis Mariae","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b1":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Lawrence of Brindisi","work":"Mariale","locus":"Sermon One, on Apocalypse 12:1 (English extract reproduced by Stanley Gahan, O.F.M. Cap.)","source_kind":"Explicit Marian commentary","verbatim_excerpt":"John speaks here of the Virgin Mother of God","source_url":"https://www.catholicculture.org/culture/library/view.cfm?recnum=2977","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Mariale","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b2":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Lawrence of Brindisi","work":"Mariale","locus":"Marian exposition reproduced in “The Woman Clothed with the Sun”","source_kind":"Explicit Marian/Coronation application","verbatim_excerpt":"She stands at the right hand of God as heaven’s exalted Queen","source_url":"https://www.catholicculture.org/culture/library/view.cfm?recnum=2977","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Mariale","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b3":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Robert Bellarmine","work":"A Commentary on the Book of Psalms","locus":"Psalm 44, verse 11","translator":"Ven. John O’Sullivan, D.D.","edition":"James Duffy & Co., 1866 English translation","source_kind":"Direct commentary with explicit Marian application","verbatim_excerpt":"If applied to the Blessed Virgin, it requires no straining","source_url":"https://www.ecatholic2000.com/bellarmine/commentary-on-psalms.shtml","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"A Commentary on the Book of Psalms","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b4":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Eudes","work":"The Admirable Heart of Mary","locus":"Part Six, Chapter I","source_kind":"Explicit Marian commentary on Psalm 44:14","verbatim_excerpt":"all her glory proceed from her Heart","source_url":"https://www.liberius.net/livres/The_admirable_Heart_of_Mary_000000374.pdf","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"The Admirable Heart of Mary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b5":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St Alphonsus Maria de Liguori","work":"The Glories of Mary","locus":"Discourse VIII, Another Discourse on the Assumption of Mary","edition":"Second American Edition, 1852 English translation","source_kind":"Explicit Marian heavenly-queenship application","verbatim_excerpt":"we ... are also queens of this kingdom, but thou art our queen","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/72411/72411-h/72411-h.htm","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"The Glories of Mary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b6":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"St John Damascene","work":"Homily on the Dormition / Assumption of the Mother of God","locus":"Heavenly reception of the Mother of God; Canticles 6:9","source_kind":"Explicit Marian Assumption application","verbatim_excerpt":"Who is she that comes forth as the morning rising, fair as the moon","source_url":"https://www.crossroadsinitiative.com/media/articles/ancient-homily-on-marys-assumption/","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Homily on the Dormition / Assumption of the Mother of God","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b7":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Pope Leo XIII","work":"Augustissimae Virginis Mariae","locus":"§12","source_kind":"Papal Marian/Rosary application of Judith 13:23–25","verbatim_excerpt":"this perennial stream of praise ... was foretold","source_url":"https://www.vatican.va/content/leo-xiii/en/encyclicals/documents/hf_l-xiii_enc_12091897_augustissimae-virginis-mariae.html","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Augustissimae Virginis Mariae","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b8":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Pope Leo XIII","work":"Augustissimae Virginis Mariae","locus":"§12","source_kind":"Papal Marian/Rosary application of Judith 13:23–25","verbatim_excerpt":"thy praise shall not depart out of the mouth of man","source_url":"https://www.vatican.va/content/leo-xiii/en/encyclicals/documents/hf_l-xiii_enc_12091897_augustissimae-virginis-mariae.html","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Augustissimae Virginis Mariae","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b9":{"kind":"supplementary_traditional_source","entry":{"author":"Thomas Worthington (citing St Fulbert), in Haydock","work":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","locus":"Judith 15:10","source_kind":"Direct commentary with explicit Marian typology","verbatim_excerpt":"Judith was a figure of the blessed Virgin, to whom these praises chiefly belong.","source_url":"https://www.studylight.org/commentaries/eng/hcc/judith-15.html","source_text_scope":"excerpt"},"source":"Haydock Catholic Bible Commentary","status":"APPROVED"},"glo5.b10":{"kind":"catena_aurea","pericope_ids":["catena.luke.1.48"],"source":"Catena Aurea","status":"APPROVED"}};
